    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think that's exactly right. I mean, I sit on two very important committees, the Appropriations Committee and the Intelligence Committee and all the House Select Committee on Intelligence, which if I just let it, that committee alone would take 80% of my time. You know, for example, next week, I'm traveling to, all through Africa, to Nigeria, to Kenya, to Ethiopia and other places, all because we know that Boko Haram and Azerbaijan and other terrorist groups are beginning to rise up to that part of Africa. So there's that element to it and that, you know, this isn't a junket by any means. I mean, I'll be traveling by myself and sitting in coach. you know, but it's important work. And then, you know, my work on the appropriations committee, we may have, you know, six hearings in a week that will last hours. And in between that time, you try to meet with constituents and you try to, you know, do the media that's important so people know what you're doing. You try to meet with other members and discuss legislation and write legislation. And really, I could keep going. There's just an awful lot to do if you're trying to be a good member.",
